  "priorExpiration": "2015-12-28",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Fis 1110.08 Miscellaneous Fees.\n\n(a) The fee for a permit to train dogs, pursuant to RSA 207:12-a, shall be $5.\n\n(b) The fee for a wholesaler’s venison license, pursuant to RSA 212:30-d, shall be $50.\n\n(c) The fee for a wildlife habitat license, pursuant to RSA 214:9, XV, shall be $2.50.\n\n(d) The fee for an educational or summer camp group fishing license, pursuant to RSA 214:9, XIII, shall be $25, in addition to the agent fee required by RSA 214-A:4, I.\n\n(e) The fee for a fur buyer’s license, pursuant to RSA 214:25, shall be $50 for residents and $150 for nonresidents.\n\n(f) The fee for a taxidermy license, pursuant to RSA 214:29-a, shall be $50.\n\nSource. #10874, EMERGENCY RULE, eff 7-1-15, EXPIRED: 12-28-15\n\nNew. #10981, eff 1-1-16; ss by by #13874, eff 2-23-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/fis1100.html"
